{"study_accession":"PRJNA1210615","secondary_study_accession":"SRP557281","title":"Characterization of the TREM-1 Signaling Landscape in Human Neutrophils","description":"The Triggering Receptor Expressed on Myeloid Cells (TREM)-1 is a member of the Immunoglobulin superfamily. Beyond its role in acute and chronic inflammatory processes, TREM-1 is also involved in cancer emergence and progression. Advanced information about the TREM-1 signaling cascade may reveal novel targets for treating inflammatory and cancer diseases. We investigated the transcriptomic profile of PMN after TREM-1 ligation that made us available to link the previously analyzed kinome activity to the resulting transcriptomic profile. In sum, we revealed several signaling pathways being active after TREM-1 ligation that are associated with various biological processed and diseases. Overall design: RNA-seq profiling of purified human PMN after TREM-1 ligation compared to an isotype matched control as well as after TLR-4 ligation compared to a medium control.","pubmed":"41785288","geo_series":"","n_samples":12,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN46250499","study_accession":"PRJNA1210615","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"PMN_isotype_3","description":"PMN_isotype_3","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM8735001","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-03-23","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood"],["tissue","peripheral blood"],["cell_type","purified neutrophils (PMN)"],["treatment","4C9"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR31997849","experiment_accession":"SRX27351037","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":36516546,"base_count":10954963800,"first_public":"2026-03-23","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM8735001: PMN_isotype_3 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"